# Local Worker secrets. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# In a deployed environment these are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET must never appear in wrangler.jsonc and must never be
# committed — it is the one credential that lets anyone mint sign-ins as us.

# The "Web application" OAuth client from Google Cloud Console → Credentials.
# Add an authorized redirect URI for every origin you sign in from, e.g.
#   http://localhost:5173/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Optional. Pins the OAuth callback origin when the Worker sits behind a proxy
# that rewrites the Host header. Defaults to the request's own origin.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN="https://nuggbudz.example.com"

# Liveness windows for the pool, in seconds. Production values live in
# wrangler.jsonc (15 min of quiet before a queue entry is dropped, 10 min before
# an unconfirmed match is cancelled). Shrink them here to watch the expiry path
# run in seconds — `pnpm smoke` runs its expiry checks only when the queue
# window is 20s or less.
# QUEUE_IDLE_SECONDS="6"
# QUEUE_WARN_LEAD_SECONDS="3"
# MATCH_CONFIRM_SECONDS="8"
